    oe:aboutDisease oed:chronic_obstructive_pulmonary_disease ;
    oe:answerText "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) often results in progressive airflow limitation and is a major cause of morbidity, mortality, and healthcare resource utilization (HCRU). Single-inhaler triple therapy with budesonide/glycopyrronium/formoterol fumarate dehydrate (BGF) is recommended for maintenance in adults with moderate-to-severe COPD not adequately controlled by dual therapy."^^xsd:string ;
